{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-score/score/pulls/3307","id":4768155057,"node_id":"PR_kwDONP32A88AAAABHDRFsQ","html_url":"https://github.com/eclipse-score/score/pull/3307","diff_url":"https://github.com/eclipse-score/score/pull/3307.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/eclipse-score/score/pull/3307.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-score/score/issues/3307","number":3307,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"docs: Complete AI tooling evaluation and selection for S-CORE","user":{"login":"jnsagai","id":20442122,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNDQyMTIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20442122?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai","html_url":"https://github.com/jnsagai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Improvement\n\n## Description\n\nComplete the AI tooling evaluation for #3115 with explicit recommendations and rationale for all eight listed options. Recommend APM for packaging, Spec Kit for integration development and Harbor for comparative evaluation. Keep S-CORE's native engineering workflow authoritative. Retain Lola as a fallback, Syspilot as the preferred subsequent native-context prototype, BMAD as an alternative, OKIT for isolated prototyping, and reviewed Pharaoh concepts without adopting its archived repository.\n\nThe native decision record preserves `dec_rec__infra__ai_sdlc_tooling`, remains `proposed`, and advances to version 3. Recommendations distinguish source-based engineering judgment from retained Spec Kit/fabric execution. Comparative deployment results, tool qualification and human acceptance are not invented.\n\nThis is a replacement candidate for the same-ID DR in #3140. Merge one representation at the current infrastructure path: accept this PR and supersede #3140, or incorporate this content there and supersede #3307. The contributor has not modified or closed another author's PR.\n\n## Related ticket\n\nCloses #3115 upon accepted merge of the evaluation decision record. Relates to #3140.\n\n## Validation and review artifacts\n\n[Complete review packet](https://github.com/Eclipse-SDV-Hackathon-Chapter-Four/Thinking_CAPs/tree/contrib/score-ai-sdlc-3115-evidence/contributions/issues/eclipse-score/score/3115/completion) includes the native source/patch, comparison and acceptance mapping, immutable source identities, exact check commands and logs, native export delta, license/qualification limits, public branch rules and reviewer handoff. The native source diff adds only the decision record. Current main already includes lifecycle link fix `6122462`; earlier failed runs are preserved.\n\nThe final local check results and hosted workflow state are recorded in `license-review/verification-report.json` and `license-review/publication.json`. Local results do not imply hosted CI success. The public main rules require passing ECA and one approval with code owner coverage; neither an agent recommendation nor a test result supplies that approval.\n\nLicense follow-up: the native DR and packet Python verifier use the exact pinned Apache-2.0 project header, with NOTICE/LICENSE retained. Explicit file-path checks cover the source files in addition to the native Bazel target; all applicable checks are rerun on the corrected head. [Current header audit and validation](https://github.com/Eclipse-SDV-Hackathon-Chapter-Four/Thinking_CAPs/tree/contrib/score-ai-sdlc-3115-evidence/contributions/issues/eclipse-score/score/3115/license-review).\n","created_at":"2026-10-07T04:59:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T17:10:58Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"8a382cb8592a465dde28f7ea4438e4eb00605bd4","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"AlexanderLanin","id":5074553,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzQ1NTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5074553?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexanderLanin","html_url":"https://github.com/AlexanderLanin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexanderLanin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexanderLanin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexanderLanin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexanderLanin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexanderLanin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexanderLanin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexanderLanin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexanderLanin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexanderLanin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"MaximilianSoerenPollak","id":74557518,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NTU3NTE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74557518?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaximilianSoerenPollak","html_url":"https://github.com/MaximilianSoerenPollak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaximilianSoerenPollak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaximilianSoerenPollak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaximilianSoerenPollak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaximilianSoerenPollak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscription